WEBVTT

00:34.659 --> 00:36.286
-Where is he?
-Hey, Ho-jin.

00:36.369 --> 00:38.038
He's been crying for an hour.

00:45.045 --> 00:45.879
Jin-suk.

00:46.546 --> 00:48.173
Get up, will you?

00:48.673 --> 00:50.216
Hey, Ho-jin.

00:50.967 --> 00:54.345
Why are you crying in public?
You're embarrassing yourself. Let's go.

00:56.514 --> 01:00.226
Guess what? Shin Ji-sun said
I broke up with her first.

01:00.310 --> 01:02.395
But I never did.

01:03.063 --> 01:06.691
She told me to think carefully,
but I swear I never did.

01:07.233 --> 01:10.612
Sure. Let's think about it at home.

01:10.695 --> 01:12.072
Come on. Up you go.

01:12.155 --> 01:14.783
I'm so angry and frustrated.

01:14.866 --> 01:16.242
When did I ever say that?

01:16.326 --> 01:18.328
I get it. Just walk straight.

01:18.411 --> 01:19.496
Okay.

01:19.996 --> 01:20.830
Walk straight.

01:34.761 --> 01:35.595
Jin-suk.

01:37.388 --> 01:39.849
Have you sobered up a bit?
Shall I drive you home?

01:42.143 --> 01:42.977
Here.

01:43.478 --> 01:45.730
I don't want it.

01:50.985 --> 01:53.696
Whenever I'd get drunk,
Ji-sun would come pick me up.

02:06.960 --> 02:07.794
What was that?

02:09.129 --> 02:11.631
I'm just so heartbroken

02:12.215 --> 02:15.635
that I'm sharing my sadness
with the world.

02:18.638 --> 02:20.223
Does that make you feel better?

02:20.306 --> 02:21.266
Yes.

02:23.184 --> 02:26.271
Expressing my emotions outwardly
makes me feel better.

02:28.481 --> 02:29.607
I bet people like you,

02:29.691 --> 02:32.277
who bottle up their feelings
and deal with them alone,

02:32.360 --> 02:33.820
would never understand.

02:34.904 --> 02:36.030
You're right.

02:36.531 --> 02:37.866
I don't understand it.

02:39.450 --> 02:42.745
Because I'd be burdening others
with my emotions.

02:44.706 --> 02:47.709
I don't understand you either,
you cold-blooded jerk.

02:52.213 --> 02:55.466
Not expressing my feelings
doesn't mean they're not there.

03:02.515 --> 03:04.517
Or that they're easy to get over.

03:21.451 --> 03:22.660
Are you posting a photo?

03:23.953 --> 03:26.831
If you are, make sure
the brand-sponsored watch is in it.

03:28.708 --> 03:31.836
By the way, Mu-hee,
Nanami reached out to me.

03:31.920 --> 03:33.755
She and Hiro arrived in Korea today.

03:34.714 --> 03:35.548
Did she?

03:36.424 --> 03:38.092
I guess he has work in Korea.

03:38.176 --> 03:40.845
She actually asked about your schedule.

03:40.929 --> 03:42.639
Maybe he's here to see you.

03:42.722 --> 03:44.432
Me? Why?

03:45.308 --> 03:47.018
Didn't you say you met Hiro on the plane?

03:47.518 --> 03:48.811
Are you sure nothing happened?

03:51.272 --> 03:52.190
Right.

03:52.982 --> 03:54.484
I did see him…

03:56.819 --> 03:59.197
but I was so out of sorts then.

04:00.198 --> 04:02.242
I crashed after a glass of wine.

04:03.076 --> 04:05.078
Maybe you slipped up while you were drunk.

04:05.954 --> 04:08.581
You were chasing Ho-jin around
like a madwoman

04:09.707 --> 04:11.542
until you totally lost it.

04:12.210 --> 04:13.378
You're right.

04:14.295 --> 04:16.381
I ran after him like a madwoman

04:17.090 --> 04:18.424
and sealed the deal.

04:21.094 --> 04:22.679
Well, if your fate is sealed,

04:23.179 --> 04:27.100
can you stop posting cloudy skies
and raindrops that look like tears?

04:27.183 --> 04:29.811
It's obvious who you posted these for,

04:29.894 --> 04:31.938
but he's not the type
to look at that stuff.

04:35.108 --> 04:35.942
Have you

04:36.943 --> 04:39.862
met Mr. Joo Ho-jin since then?

04:43.533 --> 04:46.327
I haven't seen him, but we've talked.

04:46.828 --> 04:48.037
On the phone and by text.

04:48.121 --> 04:49.414
About what?

04:50.123 --> 04:51.499
Well, you know…

04:52.750 --> 04:55.878
Hey, wait. You can't just check my phone.

04:58.172 --> 05:00.633
You even memorized my lock pattern?

05:00.717 --> 05:02.927
What… what is this?

05:04.345 --> 05:05.179
You're moving?

05:08.516 --> 05:10.184
I'm moving into Ho-jin's house.

05:11.269 --> 05:12.937
We discussed it in Canada.

05:13.604 --> 05:16.232
I told him
my housing contract fell through.

05:16.733 --> 05:19.986
He agreed to let me stay at his place
for a few months.

05:20.903 --> 05:22.905
Why didn't you tell me about this?

05:22.989 --> 05:25.533
Because I figured
you'd react just like this.

05:25.616 --> 05:28.703
You'd be pressing me for details
on how he is and what he's doing.

05:29.704 --> 05:31.122
We'll be filming soon,

05:31.205 --> 05:33.499
and, like it or not,
you'll see each other.

05:33.583 --> 05:35.501
How can you work together like this?

05:41.924 --> 05:43.718
I'm going to tonight's event alone.

05:43.801 --> 05:44.677
Don't follow me.

05:44.761 --> 05:45.595
Alone?

05:46.346 --> 05:49.223
But it's a concert
sponsored by an advertiser.

05:49.307 --> 05:50.975
I should be there to introduce you.

05:51.059 --> 05:53.770
You said you didn't want me
pressing you for details.

05:54.270 --> 05:56.147
Leave before I bite your head off.

05:56.731 --> 05:57.690
Fine. I won't come.

05:59.233 --> 06:00.860
But text me once you get there.

06:09.118 --> 06:12.288
I'm laid out, all damp like wet laundry…

06:15.166 --> 06:17.543
but he's nice and dry,

06:19.337 --> 06:21.714
put back together neatly.

06:25.843 --> 06:28.179
Are you sure Do Ra-mi was wrong
and that you won?

06:31.599 --> 06:33.059
No.

06:34.060 --> 06:35.561
I lost.

06:36.312 --> 06:37.188
Run away!

06:40.483 --> 06:42.026
I shouldn't have listened to her…

06:44.695 --> 06:46.406
and run away.

07:12.849 --> 07:15.476
Hey, cut it out already.
At this rate, I'll pop out.

07:16.853 --> 07:19.105
Why blame me
when you're the one who ran away?

07:28.614 --> 07:30.867
Jin-suk, where are you?
Are you running late?

07:32.201 --> 07:34.287
Mr. Kim's here,
and Mr. Oh from the publishing company.

07:34.370 --> 07:35.746
I'm sorry. I can't go.

07:35.830 --> 07:37.165
Come. Let's take a picture.

07:38.833 --> 07:39.667
What?

07:41.544 --> 07:43.337
You called us here tonight.

07:43.921 --> 07:47.592
You begged, saying it'd lift your mood
and that you had the invitations.

07:47.675 --> 07:50.887
And you're the one who invited
Mr. Kim and Mr. Oh as an apology.

07:50.970 --> 07:51.804
So why…

07:54.098 --> 07:54.932
can't you come?

07:56.225 --> 07:57.602
I'm at the airport.

07:57.685 --> 07:59.145
I'm headed to Santiago.

08:00.271 --> 08:01.105
What?

08:01.189 --> 08:02.273
Ji-sun was right.

08:03.524 --> 08:05.276
I did break up with her first.

08:06.569 --> 08:07.570
JIN-SUK & JI-SUN

08:10.239 --> 08:12.158
OUR STORY WILL BEGIN
UNDER THE CLEAR SKIES OF JEJU

08:12.241 --> 08:13.784
AS WE SET OFF ON A NEW JOURNEY TOGETHER…

08:13.868 --> 08:16.871
So the invitations are as you wanted.

08:16.954 --> 08:19.749
What else shall we do?
Tell me all your wedding wishes.

08:21.167 --> 08:24.420
This is all so sudden that I'm not sure
we could make anything happen.

08:24.504 --> 08:25.671
Come on now.

08:26.172 --> 08:28.508
You insisted on getting married quickly.

08:29.342 --> 08:31.928
Still, I'm not sure
we should rush things like this.

08:32.428 --> 08:35.181
Let's just get it over and done with.

08:36.057 --> 08:40.311
If we don't tie the knot right now,
I don't think I'll ever want to.

08:51.030 --> 08:53.783
Why do you want to get married?

08:53.866 --> 08:54.825
Why?

08:55.493 --> 08:56.577
You said you wanted to.

09:14.345 --> 09:15.972
I was a coward,

09:17.098 --> 09:18.140
and I'm ashamed.

09:20.226 --> 09:21.727
So I'm leaving

09:23.312 --> 09:26.857
to do some self-reflection and penance.

09:30.736 --> 09:31.904
Have a safe trip.

09:33.281 --> 09:36.158
Don't cry in public,
and don't get drunk and start yelling.

09:36.993 --> 09:37.827
Okay.

09:38.578 --> 09:40.538
My dear younger brother Ho-jin.

09:41.497 --> 09:43.165
You could do more of that yourself.

09:43.791 --> 09:44.792
Do what?

09:44.875 --> 09:48.254
The vinyl record. Why'd you stare at it
with such a sad look in your eyes?

09:52.675 --> 09:53.634
See you.

09:54.343 --> 09:55.803
I hope you have a rough time.

10:08.691 --> 10:10.735
-Good evening.
-Hello.

10:10.818 --> 10:13.571
Goodness, how are you? It's been so long.

10:13.654 --> 10:14.488
How are you?

10:14.572 --> 10:16.282
Good, very good!

10:20.870 --> 10:23.080
How come your manager isn't with you?

10:23.164 --> 10:25.708
-He had other business to attend to.
-I see.

10:26.334 --> 10:30.379
The Italian ambassador is here today.
Would you like to say hello after?

10:30.463 --> 10:31.505
That'd be an honor.

10:31.589 --> 10:33.299
Okay. I'll arrange a meeting.

10:33.382 --> 10:34.508
Thank you.

10:35.593 --> 10:37.261
Ho-jin, we have a situation.

10:37.345 --> 10:39.138
Could you please help us out?

10:39.221 --> 10:40.514
Sure. What is it?

10:41.015 --> 10:43.392
Don't. I invited him here as a guest.

10:43.476 --> 10:45.436
It'd be impolite to ask.

10:45.936 --> 10:50.775
We don't have an interpreter,
so I'm unable to greet the theater staff.

10:50.858 --> 10:52.109
They'll arrive soon enough.

10:52.610 --> 10:54.904
-They're at Chungmu-ro.
-How far can it be?

10:54.987 --> 10:56.906
Chungmu-ro is over an hour away!

10:56.989 --> 11:01.243
You've been the ambassador for how long?
Yet you still don't know Seoul geography?

11:02.078 --> 11:05.873
Isn't there anyone from the embassy
who can interpret for you?

11:05.956 --> 11:09.960
I don't think they'll make it in time
with the traffic and all.

11:13.172 --> 11:16.300
Then would you like me to help?

11:16.884 --> 11:18.094
That'd be lovely.

11:18.177 --> 11:20.554
That would be fantastic.

11:21.138 --> 11:22.640
-Thank you.
-No problem.

11:22.723 --> 11:27.645
I prepared some opening remarks
for the concert.

11:27.728 --> 11:29.605
Could you just help with those?

11:30.106 --> 11:33.818
I'll just let the people I came with know,
and then I'll get ready.

11:33.901 --> 11:35.444
Of course. Thanks a lot.

11:35.528 --> 11:37.655
You're a lifesaver. Thank you.

11:52.128 --> 11:53.921
-Do you come here often?
-Me? No.

11:54.004 --> 11:55.923
-No?
-What about you?

11:56.006 --> 11:57.425
It's my first time.

12:03.097 --> 12:04.557
Unbelievable.

12:07.852 --> 12:12.523
CAN THIS LOVE BE TRANSLATED?

12:46.849 --> 12:48.726
The rascal's not coming.

13:02.490 --> 13:05.034
Apparently, the ambassador
and his wife are also fans of Do Ra-mi.

13:06.952 --> 13:08.412
-When I greet them…
-Yes?

13:08.913 --> 13:10.956
…an interpreter will be present, right?

13:11.040 --> 13:12.249
Yes, of course.

13:13.417 --> 13:14.710
There they are.

13:15.211 --> 13:16.504
Hello.

13:25.554 --> 13:26.806
This is Ms. Cha Mu-hee.

13:38.025 --> 13:38.859
Nice to meet you.

13:39.360 --> 13:40.653
Thank you for coming.

13:41.153 --> 13:42.947
I'm a big fan of Do Ra-mi's.

13:46.575 --> 13:49.119
Thank you for inviting me.

13:54.375 --> 13:56.085
Mu-hee, you must be exhausted.

13:56.585 --> 13:57.461
Oh dear.

13:57.962 --> 14:02.466
You can skip the embassy bazaar
that the ambassador's wife invited you to.

14:05.845 --> 14:07.471
He was a different interpreter, right?

14:07.555 --> 14:08.722
Sorry?

14:09.306 --> 14:12.852
Wasn't there a different interpreter
at the start of the concert?

14:13.352 --> 14:16.021
Well, I'm not sure.

14:17.481 --> 14:18.899
Was I seeing things again?

14:20.109 --> 14:22.152
Hey, Joo Ho-jin!

14:24.613 --> 14:26.782
Where might you be, Joo Ho-jin?

14:27.283 --> 14:29.618
Something came up,
so I couldn't go to my seat.

14:30.369 --> 14:33.497
I'm in the parking lot.
Could you ride with Mr. Oh to my place?

14:33.581 --> 14:35.541
No, Mr. Oh already left.

14:36.208 --> 14:38.002
Wait for me, Joo Ho-jin.

14:39.670 --> 14:40.796
There it is.

14:44.800 --> 14:45.759
I'll be going, then.

14:46.343 --> 14:47.303
Wait, Mu-hee?

14:47.386 --> 14:48.554
Going down.

14:49.388 --> 14:50.890
Doors closing.

14:51.390 --> 14:52.391
Well, take care.

14:53.392 --> 14:54.727
Which floor?

14:57.646 --> 15:00.566
I'm going to the same floor as you.

15:00.649 --> 15:01.525
Thank you.

15:01.609 --> 15:02.776
Don't mention it.

15:05.029 --> 15:06.113
Ms. Cha Mu-hee, right?

15:08.699 --> 15:10.576
-You know me?
-Of course I do.

15:10.659 --> 15:12.578
Why, you're a famous actress.

15:14.496 --> 15:17.082
I was sitting next to you
in the concert hall earlier.

15:18.083 --> 15:19.919
Next to that empty seat.

15:20.711 --> 15:22.046
I see.

15:22.129 --> 15:23.172
Yes.

15:23.255 --> 15:25.132
And I heard what you just said.

15:25.883 --> 15:27.009
You were right.

15:28.427 --> 15:30.346
It's not the same interpreter.

15:30.971 --> 15:31.805
Sorry?

15:31.889 --> 15:35.267
I know the guy
who was interpreting at the beginning.

15:35.768 --> 15:37.853
The empty seat between us

15:38.354 --> 15:41.523
was actually his seat.

15:42.942 --> 15:44.652
And that guy is, well…

15:44.735 --> 15:46.028
Doors opening.

15:49.823 --> 15:51.158
It's that guy there.

15:51.825 --> 15:52.910
Joo Ho-jin.

15:54.536 --> 15:56.372
What took you so long?

15:56.914 --> 16:01.585
We'd planned for a dinner of four here,
but two people canceled.

16:01.669 --> 16:05.047
If someone as distinguished as you
joins us, all the better.

16:05.130 --> 16:08.717
Still, the owner of the house
didn't invite me, so…

16:08.801 --> 16:11.720
Well, this house is practically mine.

16:11.804 --> 16:13.222
It's only his on paper.

16:13.722 --> 16:14.932
It's okay.

16:17.017 --> 16:19.812
I must say, I am pretty hungry.
I'll take the free meal, then.

16:19.895 --> 16:20.896
Marvelous.

16:21.897 --> 16:23.774
Don't pay that guy any mind.

16:23.857 --> 16:26.819
Just think of him as a manservant
who works at this house.

16:31.699 --> 16:33.325
Please come in.

16:34.827 --> 16:38.539
This place will impress you.
Just look at it.

16:39.039 --> 16:43.043
The person who built this house
traveled all over the world

16:43.127 --> 16:46.380
collecting old art,
classical books, antiques,

16:46.463 --> 16:49.466
and even the vinyl records over there.

16:49.550 --> 16:53.470
This house is as good as a museum.

16:54.054 --> 16:56.348
You mean
Ho-jin's maternal grandfather, don't you?

16:56.432 --> 16:57.266
Yeah.

16:57.766 --> 16:59.518
Wait, you knew that?

17:00.019 --> 17:01.687
Have you been here before?

17:03.272 --> 17:05.024
Once, just briefly.

17:05.107 --> 17:06.316
I see.

17:06.817 --> 17:09.194
Well then, you'll feel right at home.

17:11.071 --> 17:13.699
Why are you standing around?
Get on it and make us dinner.

17:14.616 --> 17:16.577
Any preferences, Ms. Cha Mu-hee?

17:16.660 --> 17:18.662
I'm not too picky,

17:19.163 --> 17:20.581
but I do love spicy food.

17:20.664 --> 17:21.957
Spicy food?

17:22.541 --> 17:24.835
Did you get that?
Anything spicy on the menu?

17:24.918 --> 17:27.254
Jin-suk chose tonight's menu,
and it's Japanese.

17:27.337 --> 17:29.339
Japanese? Forget that.

17:29.423 --> 17:32.051
Just do a spicy braised monkfish
or stir-fried octopus.

17:32.134 --> 17:34.136
-How does that sound?
-Sounds great.

17:34.219 --> 17:35.262
That works, right?

17:35.345 --> 17:37.139
No, I don't have monkfish or octopus.

17:37.222 --> 17:38.307
-Any blue crab?
-None.

17:38.390 --> 17:39.266
-Cod?
-Nope.

17:39.349 --> 17:40.476
Squid, then?

17:40.559 --> 17:41.435
-I don't--
-You do!

17:41.518 --> 17:42.352
-You do!
-I don't.

17:42.436 --> 17:44.605
Then stir-fried squid it is.
Make it spicy.

17:45.397 --> 17:47.399
-How does that sound?
-Sounds great.

18:00.287 --> 18:02.956
He's even a good cook, you know.

18:03.499 --> 18:06.543
-I know.
-My, my, you know everything!

18:06.627 --> 18:08.504
You're a match made in… One moment.

18:09.463 --> 18:11.215
Excuse me. I should get this.

18:12.716 --> 18:14.093
Yes, Mr. Oh?

18:43.413 --> 18:45.582
Mr. Oh, don't come here. Go back.

18:45.666 --> 18:49.378
I'm almost there.
I even brought Jeong, like you asked.

18:49.461 --> 18:51.463
Just turn around! Don't come here.

19:10.190 --> 19:11.984
Mr. Joo, can I help with anything?

19:16.947 --> 19:18.490
Should I chop this up?

19:19.908 --> 19:21.785
Go sit down. You're Mr. Kim's guest.

19:30.002 --> 19:31.503
Why are you even here anyway?

19:33.338 --> 19:35.632
Mr. Kim asked me to come,

19:37.009 --> 19:38.093
so I'm here for dinner.

19:40.053 --> 19:41.430
I'm just so hungry.

19:42.514 --> 19:43.432
Is that right?

19:43.515 --> 19:45.267
Sure. Let's say you're really hungry.

19:46.560 --> 19:49.146
Though, by my logic,
you'd have to be starving to be here.

19:54.526 --> 19:55.611
Oh my!

19:56.820 --> 19:58.238
What's this?

19:58.989 --> 20:00.282
It looks delicious.

20:01.366 --> 20:03.827
It's just kelp broth.
I haven't even started cooking.

20:04.453 --> 20:05.287
So it is.

20:07.456 --> 20:08.457
Just like us.

20:11.168 --> 20:14.379
We're like broth with nothing but kelp.
Not even started yet.

20:20.260 --> 20:23.555
Stop hovering here and go sit down.
I'll feed you.

20:27.809 --> 20:28.894
You turned it off?

20:29.603 --> 20:31.480
Because I need to let it cool.

20:32.314 --> 20:33.357
It's for seasoning.

20:36.068 --> 20:37.945
Mr. Joo Ho-jin?

20:39.446 --> 20:40.447
I get that

20:41.490 --> 20:44.326
I kept sneaking little sips of kelp broth

20:44.826 --> 20:47.412
and turned off the heat prematurely.

20:49.289 --> 20:52.668
But can't we let it boil a little longer
instead of letting it cool?

20:54.378 --> 20:56.421
It'd be a waste to stop
after just a taste.

20:57.589 --> 20:59.299
It would be a shame, wouldn't it?

21:02.552 --> 21:05.639
I think I turned it off
and left it to cool at the perfect time.

21:06.139 --> 21:07.975
It's not a waste nor a shame.

21:08.058 --> 21:11.520
I mean, it's just water with kelp.
There's nothing to it, really.

21:15.315 --> 21:16.942
That's not true.

21:18.944 --> 21:19.820
I did

21:21.154 --> 21:22.781
kiss you once!

21:32.416 --> 21:33.959
I was going to fry this.

21:42.884 --> 21:44.886
The concert must be over by now.

21:44.970 --> 21:47.055
Should I try contacting Ms. Cha Mu-hee?

21:47.139 --> 21:49.224
No. There's no need.

21:49.308 --> 21:52.936
Once she finds out I'm in Seoul,
she'll get in touch.

21:53.020 --> 21:57.357
Why not just reach out to her first?
You did come all this way to see her.

21:58.108 --> 22:00.444
Nanami, I didn't come here
to meet that zombie.

22:00.527 --> 22:01.945
I came to take photographs.

22:02.529 --> 22:04.865
Look.
Aren't the fall night lights beautiful?

22:05.532 --> 22:08.243
You can take pictures of fall scenery
anywhere in Japan.

22:09.036 --> 22:10.078
It's different.

22:10.162 --> 22:12.456
The cityscape is completely different.

22:12.539 --> 22:14.958
-You can see it through the camera.
-Sure.

22:15.042 --> 22:17.544
So you won't meet Ms. Cha Mu-hee
before you leave?

22:19.463 --> 22:21.757
If she contacts me,

22:22.382 --> 22:25.135
I guess I could see her while I'm here.

22:34.269 --> 22:37.314
It's spicy and delicious.
Man, you're good.

22:37.397 --> 22:39.316
You should've gone on Culinary Class Wars.

22:40.692 --> 22:43.862
I went on that family trip to Canada, too,
back when he was young.

22:44.446 --> 22:46.865
So I guess you really are like family.

22:46.948 --> 22:48.283
There's no doubt about it.

22:48.784 --> 22:51.161
Did you visit that park
we went to back then?

22:51.244 --> 22:53.789
-That's where they were filming.
-Is that so?

22:53.872 --> 22:56.917
Then did you visit
where we saw the double rainbow?

22:57.000 --> 22:58.168
That waterfall.

23:02.381 --> 23:04.966
I wanted to, but I couldn't find it.

23:05.050 --> 23:08.762
That's too bad.
It was such a splendid waterfall.

23:11.973 --> 23:13.892
A waterfall only you and I know about.

23:15.519 --> 23:17.145
The waterfall is nice and cool.

23:35.038 --> 23:37.207
The waterfall we saw together

23:37.999 --> 23:39.501
was pretty too.

23:42.045 --> 23:43.380
It wasn't a waterfall.

23:45.382 --> 23:47.426
But we agreed to call it one.

23:47.926 --> 23:52.264
I'm done humoring your claim
that all falling water is a waterfall.

24:00.147 --> 24:01.106
Hey.

24:01.940 --> 24:03.525
About the concert.

24:04.734 --> 24:07.696
Did you come to interpret
because you knew I was coming?

24:10.991 --> 24:12.617
What are you thinking?

24:13.201 --> 24:15.996
Why would I go there to interpret,
knowing you'd be there?

24:16.079 --> 24:19.040
You did that once before to meet me.

24:19.624 --> 24:20.542
The answer is no.

24:27.174 --> 24:28.550
Then why didn't you come sit?

24:31.261 --> 24:32.721
I thought it'd be awkward.

24:33.305 --> 24:35.557
Then why did you agree
to let Yong-u move in?

24:35.640 --> 24:37.100
If he's here, I'll come by often.

24:37.184 --> 24:40.437
According to Yong-u,
you've never been to his place,

24:40.937 --> 24:42.772
so you'd never show up here.

24:43.690 --> 24:44.691
That's true.

24:46.276 --> 24:47.110
Fine.

24:50.197 --> 24:52.657
So you came here
with those mistaken assumptions?

24:52.741 --> 24:54.242
With such confidence?

24:56.369 --> 24:58.914
I need that confidence
to be able to sway you again.

24:59.623 --> 25:00.665
You see,

25:01.458 --> 25:03.126
rather than walk away with dignity,

25:03.210 --> 25:05.712
I've decided to be the crazy bitch
who sways you.

25:06.254 --> 25:07.088
Because…

25:10.592 --> 25:13.929
I'm placing my hope in the last thing
you said to me that day.

25:21.686 --> 25:23.313
You said you were going to cross.

25:27.400 --> 25:28.485
So…

25:31.780 --> 25:33.406
we did see a waterfall together!

26:06.439 --> 26:09.526
I ought to visit a place like that
at least once before I die.

26:10.735 --> 26:11.570
You have though.

26:12.320 --> 26:16.157
One of our drones fell into a ravine,
and you and I fished it out. Remember?

26:17.867 --> 26:19.369
Oh yeah, we did.

26:19.911 --> 26:22.372
That was so rough.
I said I'd never go back.

26:22.455 --> 26:23.915
But it looks great like this.

26:23.999 --> 26:27.002
That's why they say
it's a comedy from afar

26:27.085 --> 26:29.504
but a tragedy from up close.

26:30.005 --> 26:33.550
The real tragedy is all the footage
we haven't even started reviewing yet.

26:33.633 --> 26:36.261
My eyes are watering
like they're about to pop out.

26:36.344 --> 26:38.597
Don't cry.

26:39.389 --> 26:42.142
Yong-u, thanks
for always bringing the snacks.

26:42.225 --> 26:44.686
Mu-hee looks great, so don't you worry.

26:45.270 --> 26:46.980
Thank you. And hang in there!

26:47.063 --> 26:49.399
-I'll clean up before I leave.
-You don't need to.

26:49.899 --> 26:52.527
We should save some macarons
for Producer Shin.

26:52.611 --> 26:54.613
Looks like another all-nighter for her.

26:54.696 --> 26:57.449
Starting tomorrow,
she should be free during the day.

26:57.532 --> 26:59.200
Her fiancé went to Spain.

26:59.993 --> 27:01.786
Spain? The writer Na Jin-suk?

27:02.287 --> 27:05.373
Yeah, he posted on Instagram
that he's going to Spain. Santiago.

27:05.457 --> 27:06.750
I'm so freaking jealous.

27:07.334 --> 27:09.461
Well, we're going to Italy.

27:09.544 --> 27:11.671
We're going for work. Not to have fun.

27:27.312 --> 27:30.565
NA JIN-SUK
#SPAIN #SANTIAGO #CAMINO

28:07.227 --> 28:08.269
Wow.

28:08.770 --> 28:10.772
So she really is going around
trying to cheat.

28:14.275 --> 28:15.527
Hello, sir.

28:16.027 --> 28:17.904
-To Yeonnam-dong, please.
-Sure.

28:24.744 --> 28:25.578
Yes, Mr. Ahn.

28:26.079 --> 28:27.580
I swung by the cutting room.

28:28.081 --> 28:29.124
Of course!

28:29.708 --> 28:32.544
-They say the Canada footage looks great.
-Yong-u.

28:32.627 --> 28:34.754
-They were singing her praises.
-My bag, Yong-u!

28:35.547 --> 28:38.717
Italy has a totally different vibe
from Canada,

28:39.217 --> 28:40.510
so it should feel fresh.

28:41.094 --> 28:45.348
Sorry. I was on the phone with my boss,
so I couldn't answer your call.

28:46.307 --> 28:47.308
It's fine.

28:48.393 --> 28:49.561
Is that for working late?

28:53.773 --> 28:54.607
Those clothes.

28:55.233 --> 28:57.986
I meant, are those clothes
for you to wear while editing?

28:58.945 --> 29:00.447
Not "work late" as in cheating.

29:02.532 --> 29:03.408
Sure.

29:03.908 --> 29:05.535
Both outfits are for working late.

29:06.494 --> 29:07.620
Right.

29:07.704 --> 29:09.497
Editing and cheating.

29:09.998 --> 29:12.125
You must be busy keeping up with both.

29:13.418 --> 29:14.753
Did you hurt yourself?

29:28.183 --> 29:30.143
ATFL tears can be quite serious.

29:33.188 --> 29:34.522
An "ATFL tear"?

29:34.606 --> 29:36.775
I told you I was an athlete.

29:37.317 --> 29:40.236
It'll feel a bit better if you tape it.
Shall I do it for you?

30:00.298 --> 30:01.549
Are you okay?

30:02.050 --> 30:02.884
What?

30:03.593 --> 30:04.427
Right.

30:05.261 --> 30:06.387
I couldn't tell earlier,

30:07.263 --> 30:08.556
but it's starting to hurt.

30:10.099 --> 30:11.100
Let me see.

30:32.580 --> 30:34.541
-Does that hurt?
-Yeah.

30:51.015 --> 30:55.520
Is an ATFL tear
something I should be worried about?

30:57.272 --> 30:59.607
It's just a fancy term
for a sprained ankle.

31:00.108 --> 31:01.693
Otherwise, you would've limped off.

31:07.407 --> 31:10.410
You said you were an athlete, didn't you?
Which sport?

31:10.493 --> 31:13.246
-Shooting.
-Did you do it for long?

31:15.498 --> 31:18.626
I did it until I was conscripted.
An injury ended my career.

31:19.586 --> 31:22.338
After the army,
my mom got me a job at her brother's firm.

31:24.674 --> 31:26.676
Your mom's brother's company?

31:28.177 --> 31:30.221
Then the CEO of your company is…

31:30.305 --> 31:33.349
Yes. CEO Ahn is my uncle.

31:34.017 --> 31:35.560
So you were family.

31:36.060 --> 31:37.228
That explains it.

31:37.770 --> 31:40.982
I wondered why a fresh-faced rookie
was working with Ms. Cha Mu-hee.

31:41.482 --> 31:43.610
I might've gotten the job
through nepotism,

31:43.693 --> 31:46.279
but I've been with Mu-hee
since she was a nobody.

31:46.779 --> 31:50.617
I cried with her, clutching her script
after every failed audition.

31:51.868 --> 31:55.496
Sorry. I take back calling you
a fresh-faced rookie.

31:55.997 --> 31:59.375
In that case, take back what you said
about planning to cheat too.

32:01.419 --> 32:04.464
Now that I know what I know,
it really bothers me whenever I see you.

32:07.717 --> 32:10.595
Were you keeping me occupied
to stop me from cheating?

32:11.095 --> 32:12.847
While going on about ATFL or whatever?

32:12.931 --> 32:13.890
That

32:15.058 --> 32:17.435
was because I knew you were hurt today.

32:18.561 --> 32:20.438
I wish I didn't know, but I do.

32:21.356 --> 32:22.607
I heard he flew out today.

32:27.820 --> 32:31.074
You said you'd cheat so you couldn't
go back to him, didn't you?

32:32.659 --> 32:35.536
If you're struggling to move on,
why not just take him back?

32:36.537 --> 32:39.874
You're so out of it that you lost your bag
and sprained your ankle.

32:40.500 --> 32:44.629
You didn't even get to cheat, and tonight,
you'll be in the cutting room all night.

32:45.838 --> 32:47.090
Honestly, it's quite sad.

32:49.008 --> 32:50.510
Are you that worried about me?

32:53.054 --> 32:54.389
Then will you help me?

32:56.224 --> 32:58.059
You're clearly interested in me.

32:58.559 --> 32:59.852
After I said I'd cheat,

32:59.936 --> 33:02.355
haven't you been hanging around,
hoping for a shot?

33:07.527 --> 33:10.321
Okay, then. What if I agree to help?
What will you do about it?

33:11.990 --> 33:13.449
I'm a joke to you, aren't I?

33:13.533 --> 33:16.494
It's not that you're a joke.
I'm saying you can't do this.

33:16.577 --> 33:17.412
Why not?

33:20.999 --> 33:25.044
When a shooting athlete aims at a target,
it needs to be done with sincerity.

33:31.175 --> 33:34.679
"I'll hit the target no matter what.
If I miss, I'll be the one who gets shot."

33:36.180 --> 33:37.015
But

33:38.641 --> 33:40.643
you don't have that sincerity.

33:41.310 --> 33:45.231
That's why when it's time to fire,
you hesitate and can't pull the trigger.

34:10.173 --> 34:11.799
Thanks for your help.

34:19.223 --> 34:20.558
You pulled the trigger.

34:55.384 --> 34:56.844
Should I just contact Ms. Cha?

34:56.928 --> 34:58.137
Don't!

34:58.721 --> 35:00.598
No matter what, don't contact her first!

35:01.641 --> 35:04.393
I'm not meeting that zombie
until she asks to see me.

35:06.395 --> 35:07.313
Sure.

35:13.653 --> 35:14.987
Cha Mu-hee.

35:15.696 --> 35:17.615
Why isn't she calling me?

35:18.407 --> 35:22.328
After what she did to me
on the plane that day…

35:24.372 --> 35:25.915
You seem okay.

35:37.677 --> 35:40.680
Hiro, it's too cold out.

35:57.071 --> 35:58.781
Shall we eat too?

35:59.657 --> 36:00.825
It'd warm us up.

36:02.326 --> 36:03.327
No, thanks.

36:12.170 --> 36:14.338
Ms. Cha Mu-hee

36:15.006 --> 36:16.591
has not reached out.

36:23.681 --> 36:24.974
Let's go back to the hotel.

36:31.272 --> 36:32.523
TO CEO OH SEONG-CHEOL

36:32.607 --> 36:35.067
TO CHA MU-HEE,
THE MOST BEAUTIFUL WOMAN IN THE UNIVERSE

36:42.200 --> 36:43.534
Here.

36:44.619 --> 36:47.538
Next time, I'll give you Do Ra-mi merch
with proper autographs.

36:47.622 --> 36:49.040
Oh, that would be great.

36:49.123 --> 36:50.708
Here. This is my book.

36:50.791 --> 36:52.126
Thank you.

36:52.919 --> 36:55.213
This is my first time meeting a novelist.

36:55.296 --> 36:56.422
No, it isn't.

36:58.007 --> 36:58.925
You've met him.

37:00.051 --> 37:01.510
You mean Mr. Joo Ho-jin?

37:03.179 --> 37:05.181
Mr. Joo Ho-jin, you wrote a book?

37:05.264 --> 37:07.308
Just once, in college.

37:07.892 --> 37:11.938
But it won a prize
and even became a bestseller.

37:13.064 --> 37:15.233
What's the title? I'd like to buy a copy.

37:15.316 --> 37:17.026
You can't get it. It's out of print.

37:17.109 --> 37:18.611
I have a few copies.

37:18.694 --> 37:20.947
Come by my studio sometime.

37:21.030 --> 37:22.615
-I'll give you one.
-Thank you.

37:24.450 --> 37:26.953
Can I post a photo on Instagram
of this book you signed?

37:27.036 --> 37:29.330
I'd be so grateful if you did.

37:30.122 --> 37:33.417
I follow you on Instagram.
Should we follow each other?

37:34.293 --> 37:36.170
I would really love to,

37:36.254 --> 37:39.006
but if we do,
your account could get a lot of heat.

37:39.590 --> 37:40.883
Is that so?

37:42.635 --> 37:44.595
So you and Ho-jin don't follow each other?

37:44.679 --> 37:46.389
Mr. Joo Ho-jin doesn't follow me.

37:46.472 --> 37:47.765
Sure, he does.

37:50.017 --> 37:51.060
Right?

37:51.686 --> 37:53.312
Ho-jin, you follow her, don't you?

37:53.980 --> 37:55.815
I saw it on your account.

37:57.400 --> 38:00.653
Mr. Joo Ho-jin, you're following me?

38:01.821 --> 38:02.780
We made that bet

38:03.322 --> 38:04.657
back in Japan.

38:05.157 --> 38:06.909
I followed you, as promised.

38:07.702 --> 38:08.995
See?

38:10.621 --> 38:12.164
I see.

38:15.001 --> 38:16.252
I had no idea.

38:16.836 --> 38:18.587
Wait, you didn't know that?

38:18.671 --> 38:21.132
I have quite a few followers, so…

38:27.346 --> 38:28.681
Oh boy, Joo Ho-jin!

38:28.764 --> 38:30.391
You were just one of many!

38:32.476 --> 38:34.770
Look. I'm sorry.

38:34.854 --> 38:37.481
As we promised that day,
I should follow you back,

38:37.982 --> 38:38.983
but it'd be a little--

38:39.066 --> 38:40.776
You don't have to. Please don't.

38:40.860 --> 38:43.696
You should've accepted
when she first offered.

38:45.823 --> 38:48.576
If the two of you are done with your tea,
you should go.

38:48.659 --> 38:50.661
No, I haven't finished my tea yet.

38:50.745 --> 38:52.288
Mu-hee, take your time with that.

38:52.371 --> 38:54.248
Mr. Kim, the time is…

38:54.332 --> 38:55.416
The time?

38:56.542 --> 38:59.587
This is the time?
It's almost time for my show to air.

38:59.670 --> 39:02.548
-Divorce Your Husband.
-You watch that too, Mr. Kim?

39:02.631 --> 39:06.344
Goodness, of course! It's excellent.
I always bawl my eyes out.

39:06.427 --> 39:08.929
-Exactly.
-Why don't we watch some TV together?

39:09.013 --> 39:10.389
-Shall we?
-Let's.

39:11.223 --> 39:13.517
Wait. Where did I put my glasses?

39:14.101 --> 39:16.145
I think I left them in your car earlier.

39:28.449 --> 39:31.786
You seem to be enjoying yourself,
but you should call it a day and go home.

39:33.996 --> 39:34.830
Yeah?

39:37.124 --> 39:39.502
Then, since I'm out here anyway,
I'll get going.

39:42.129 --> 39:44.590
Head on in. Don't leave her all alone.

39:44.673 --> 39:45.508
Mr. Kim.

39:45.591 --> 39:48.928
You left your seat empty earlier
to avoid her, didn't you?

39:50.638 --> 39:53.933
Do you find that young lady hard to read?

40:00.773 --> 40:04.110
You once told me that every person
speaks their own language.

40:04.777 --> 40:05.736
I did.

40:07.446 --> 40:09.740
I don't think
I understand her language very well.

40:13.327 --> 40:16.997
I approached thinking she was interested,
but she turned me down.

40:18.582 --> 40:20.501
I avoided her, taking that as rejection,

40:21.001 --> 40:23.170
but now she's here, acting like that.

40:25.297 --> 40:28.926
Is she interested in me again,
or does she feel bad for turning me down?

40:30.428 --> 40:31.637
I can't really tell.

40:38.894 --> 40:41.605
I have no idea what to say to her
once I'm inside.

40:43.149 --> 40:45.901
It must be frustrating
not being able to understand her.

40:47.027 --> 40:47.987
But

40:49.071 --> 40:52.700
are you fine with not understanding her?
Aren't you an interpreter?

40:54.243 --> 40:57.371
If it's a language you don't know,
you should study it.

40:57.872 --> 40:59.248
The vocabulary, syntax,

40:59.331 --> 41:03.085
and punctuation will all differ
from those of the language you speak.

41:04.795 --> 41:09.133
Look closely
and try your best to understand.

42:28.170 --> 42:29.505
The weather is lovely.

42:32.800 --> 42:34.552
Isn't the song lovely too?

44:06.143 --> 44:07.645
Mr. Joo Ho-jin.

44:08.812 --> 44:11.023
I'm going to head off now.

44:12.441 --> 44:13.776
Where's Mr. Kim?

44:13.859 --> 44:14.735
He left.

44:14.818 --> 44:16.987
I didn't even get to say goodbye.

44:19.031 --> 44:21.909
Thanks so much for dinner.
It was delicious.

44:21.992 --> 44:22.951
I'll be going.

44:23.535 --> 44:24.370
One second.

44:29.124 --> 44:29.958
We need to talk.

44:34.755 --> 44:36.465
Why are you so jittery?

44:46.767 --> 44:47.726
What is that?

44:49.395 --> 44:50.396
That.

44:51.897 --> 44:54.274
What? It's the book
Mr. Kim gave me earlier. Why?

44:54.358 --> 44:55.776
Something's up. Let me see.

44:55.859 --> 44:56.777
What? This is mine.

44:56.860 --> 44:58.821
-You're clearly hiding something.
-What?

44:58.904 --> 44:59.780
-Let's see.
-What?

44:59.863 --> 45:00.948
What's that over there?

45:10.624 --> 45:11.959
Wow.

45:14.420 --> 45:17.339
Okay, I stole it.
How'd you even see that, Eagle Eyes?

45:18.882 --> 45:20.968
I looked closely
with the intention of studying

45:22.261 --> 45:23.387
and caught a thief.

45:29.977 --> 45:32.521
You really have a knack…

45:35.190 --> 45:36.984
for driving me insane.

45:39.486 --> 45:42.114
If you're not going to turn me in,
can I have my book back?

45:42.197 --> 45:43.907
I'm embarrassed and just want to go.

46:02.760 --> 46:04.094
You're giving me this?

46:05.179 --> 46:06.180
It was always yours.

46:08.599 --> 46:10.559
I bought it as a gift for you.

46:11.685 --> 46:15.314
I didn't think I'd get to give it to you,
but here you are, stealing it yourself.

46:21.111 --> 46:21.945
Thank you.

46:23.572 --> 46:25.616
For dinner and the gift.

46:26.658 --> 46:29.369
I should repay you
for what you've given me.

46:30.954 --> 46:34.166
I'll treat you to a delicious meal
and give you a gift next time.

46:35.042 --> 46:35.876
Next time?

46:41.006 --> 46:41.882
Yong-u!

46:42.549 --> 46:44.635
You said Yong-u's moving in here.

46:45.344 --> 46:46.386
At the housewarming,

46:46.470 --> 46:49.306
I'll bring some good food and a gift.

46:50.891 --> 46:52.226
Then see you next time.

46:59.900 --> 47:01.109
Next time?

47:17.417 --> 47:18.919
She left this behind.

47:36.270 --> 47:38.730
Oh no. I only brought the sleeve.

47:42.818 --> 47:44.611
Am I an idiot?

47:47.447 --> 47:54.454
PAPAGO♥

48:03.130 --> 48:05.424
You took the sleeve
and left the record behind.

48:05.924 --> 48:07.593
Will you steal this next time?

48:08.135 --> 48:11.013
I forgot because I was in a rush to leave.

48:12.389 --> 48:13.807
It may be hard to believe,

48:13.891 --> 48:16.351
but I didn't leave it behind
on purpose this time.

48:16.435 --> 48:17.644
How far did you get?

48:19.605 --> 48:22.357
I'm almost home.

48:22.441 --> 48:25.235
Then wait in front of your place.
I'll bring it to you.

48:26.236 --> 48:27.529
Sorry? What?

48:28.280 --> 48:29.114
Now?

48:29.197 --> 48:30.282
Yes.

48:30.991 --> 48:32.075
Send me your address.

48:33.285 --> 48:34.745
I'll head over there now.

48:35.954 --> 48:39.458
You don't have to go out of your way
to come here.

48:40.250 --> 48:42.461
I'm already in my car. Should I get out?

48:42.544 --> 48:45.756
No. If you're in your car anyway,
you might as well come.

48:45.839 --> 48:47.174
I'm coming. Wait for me.

50:02.916 --> 50:04.001
Mu-hee?

50:25.230 --> 50:26.648
Your uncle is here.

50:53.884 --> 50:56.595
PAPAGO♥

51:12.360 --> 51:13.737
Your call cannot be completed.

51:13.820 --> 51:18.325
You will be forwarded to voicemail
and charged after the beep.

51:25.957 --> 51:27.334
Your call cannot be completed.

51:27.417 --> 51:30.712
You will be forwarded to voicemail
and charged after the beep.

51:40.680 --> 51:47.687
JOO HO-JIN

51:51.399 --> 51:52.400
Hey, Mr. Joo.

51:53.443 --> 51:54.986
Why is it so hard to reach you?

51:55.737 --> 51:58.907
Oh, things were so hectic
that I didn't notice my phone was dead.

51:58.990 --> 52:00.784
Have you been calling? I'm sorry.

52:01.368 --> 52:04.121
I think something's up with Ms. Cha.
I can't reach her.

52:04.204 --> 52:05.664
Mu-hee?

52:06.581 --> 52:08.083
She's at a photo shoot right now.

52:09.584 --> 52:11.753
-What?
-She's getting her hair and makeup done.

52:14.214 --> 52:15.048
Wanna talk to her?

52:16.466 --> 52:19.177
No. As long as she's okay, it's fine.

52:19.678 --> 52:22.222
Actually, an article was published today.

52:22.305 --> 52:25.725
It covers a touchy subject for her,
so I guess she didn't answer.

52:26.852 --> 52:28.019
But don't worry.

52:29.437 --> 52:30.897
She's still her cheerful self.

52:33.066 --> 52:33.984
She is?

52:50.584 --> 52:53.420
PAPAGO♥

53:07.934 --> 53:11.313
I knew things were tense with your family,
but that article was a surprise.

53:12.647 --> 53:14.733
Reporters showed up at my uncle's house.

53:15.859 --> 53:20.405
I'm under his family register.
I guess they thought they were my parents.

53:20.488 --> 53:22.115
THE GLAMOROUS FAMILY HISTORY
OF AN ACTRESS BORN INTO WEALTH

53:22.199 --> 53:25.160
But the article is in your favor.
Claims you were born into wealth.

53:25.243 --> 53:28.872
These days, being bold and fabulous works.
Everyone loves you even more.

53:29.539 --> 53:31.374
Cha Mu-hee is loved.

53:32.375 --> 53:33.335
Is that right?

53:36.338 --> 53:37.714
That's good.

53:42.552 --> 53:45.472
By the way, Ho-jin called.

53:45.972 --> 53:48.058
He was worried that he couldn't reach you.

53:48.141 --> 53:49.726
Did the two of you plan to meet up?

53:52.229 --> 53:53.855
I wanted to…

53:56.149 --> 53:57.317
but I won't be seeing him.

53:58.068 --> 53:59.653
I stood him up.

54:56.126 --> 54:57.377
Do you really

54:58.128 --> 55:01.965
not remember what happened
to your mom and dad?

55:15.979 --> 55:17.063
No smiling!

55:18.857 --> 55:19.899
You disgust me.

55:53.558 --> 55:54.392
That's me.

55:57.145 --> 55:59.230
That picture was taken on my birthday.

56:01.483 --> 56:02.692
That's my house.

56:03.902 --> 56:05.653
The flowers I grew

56:06.446 --> 56:07.489
and my chicks.

56:08.782 --> 56:10.784
Dad came home
for the first time in a while

56:12.035 --> 56:13.828
with a birthday present for me.

56:16.790 --> 56:17.999
Mu-hee!

56:18.083 --> 56:20.794
-Happy birthday to you
-Daddy!

56:20.877 --> 56:23.421
-Happy birthday to you
-A teddy bear? I love it!

56:23.505 --> 56:25.006
-Happy birthday!
-It's so cute.

56:27.342 --> 56:28.635
You're the best, Dad!

56:41.523 --> 56:43.066
Eat up.

56:43.900 --> 56:44.901
You're so cute.

57:13.096 --> 57:14.180
Mom?

57:45.837 --> 57:48.256
Serves you right, you liar.

57:53.094 --> 57:54.387
You sneaky devil.

57:54.888 --> 57:57.724
You lied,
pretending you didn't remember a thing,

57:57.807 --> 57:59.726
and now you're scared you'll get caught.

58:04.189 --> 58:05.523
You felt uneasy, didn't you?

58:06.232 --> 58:08.109
When people started loving
the likes of you.

58:08.776 --> 58:10.361
You don't believe it, do you?

58:10.904 --> 58:12.280
That they'll keep loving you.

58:17.535 --> 58:19.496
I only emerged because you're so pathetic.

58:23.458 --> 58:27.045
Leave it all to me.
After all, everyone loves Do Ra-mi.

58:50.902 --> 58:53.071
Ms. Cha Mu-hee, shall we begin?

58:53.154 --> 58:54.030
Sure.

59:02.997 --> 59:05.583
She still hasn't reached out.
What should I do?

59:10.004 --> 59:10.964
Just call her.

59:11.464 --> 59:12.674
And set up a meeting.

59:13.508 --> 59:16.886
I debated leaving,
but I'm just too curious.

59:18.721 --> 59:19.764
Let's do this!

59:21.432 --> 59:22.934
I'm curious too.

59:23.017 --> 59:23.851
About what?

59:24.727 --> 59:27.772
What happened between you
and Ms. Cha Mu-hee on the plane?

59:38.908 --> 59:40.201
I choose you.

01:00:14.736 --> 01:00:15.737
What are you doing?

01:00:18.281 --> 01:00:21.993
I'm watching the Do Ra-mi movie
to get some footage of Mu-hee.

01:00:22.744 --> 01:00:25.496
But this… I'm watching it again,
and it's still terrifying.

01:00:26.164 --> 01:00:28.666
Of course it is.
She's a zombie. A killer zombie.

01:00:29.751 --> 01:00:32.962
Yeah, she kills way too many people.

01:00:33.796 --> 01:00:36.799
But Do Ra-mi herself
only kills one person.

01:00:38.509 --> 01:00:40.178
The man she loved.

01:01:23.930 --> 01:01:25.014
Mr. Kim?

01:01:27.600 --> 01:01:29.018
Mr. Kim, is that you?

01:02:03.636 --> 01:02:04.721
Ma'am?

01:02:11.185 --> 01:02:13.479
Today's not the day you usually come

01:02:15.106 --> 01:02:16.107
to clean.

01:02:29.704 --> 01:02:30.621
Ms. Cha Mu-hee?

01:02:32.248 --> 01:02:33.374
What are you doing here?

01:02:39.213 --> 01:02:40.757
If I tell you to wait,

01:02:41.257 --> 01:02:44.051
wait in the spot I told you to wait
until I show up.

01:02:50.057 --> 01:02:52.852
I don't know
what vibe you're going for today,

01:02:54.020 --> 01:02:56.105
but I won't be humoring you anymore.

01:02:56.689 --> 01:02:57.523
Please leave.

01:02:59.442 --> 01:03:02.153
Vibe? I like that kind of thing.

01:03:04.155 --> 01:03:07.658
Yesterday's vibe was "beggar thief."
What do I seem like today?

01:03:08.868 --> 01:03:09.702
Have a guess.

01:03:12.079 --> 01:03:12.955
Are you unwell?

01:03:15.958 --> 01:03:17.001
See? You're so kind.

01:03:17.084 --> 01:03:18.252
I wasn't being kind.

01:03:18.336 --> 01:03:21.839
No, you're kind.
That's why she's pining for you.

01:03:30.181 --> 01:03:33.351
"I felt like I might die
if someone was kind to me."

01:03:35.311 --> 01:03:38.481
"It felt like kindness might kill me."

01:03:48.282 --> 01:03:49.325
Not me though.

01:03:51.410 --> 01:03:52.620
I…

01:04:01.504 --> 01:04:02.713
simply kill.

01:04:05.925 --> 01:04:07.468
And who exactly

01:04:09.220 --> 01:04:10.263
are you?

01:04:14.183 --> 01:04:15.685
Today's vibe…

01:04:18.187 --> 01:04:19.230
is Do Ra-mi.

01:04:29.699 --> 01:04:32.660
CAN THIS LOVE BE TRANSLATED?

01:06:52.967 --> 01:06:57.972
Subtitle translation by: Jimin Choi
